  "Description": {
    "DefaultText": "Decreases if you're thirsty, recovers on its own if you're not. At low levels it can cause headaches and increase fatigue. Prolonged dehydration can lead to lowered blood pressure, altered mind states and eventual death.",
    "Text": "口渴时会减少，不渴时会恢复。较低水平的水分会引发头痛和疲劳。长期脱水会导致血压降低、精神失常，最终导致死亡。",
    "zh": "口渴时会减少，不渴时会恢复。较低水平的水分会引发头痛和疲劳。长期脱水会导致血压降低、精神失常，最终导致死亡。",
    "en": "Decreases if you're thirsty, recovers on its own if you're not. At low levels it can cause headaches and increase fatigue. Prolonged dehydration can lead to lowered blood pressure, altered mind states and eventual death.",
    "ja": "喉が乾いたら減る。乾いてなければ勝手に回復する。低いと頭痛と疲労の原因になる。長時間脱水が続くと、血圧が下がり、精神状態が変わり、死に至る可能性がある。"
  },
